<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:48Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Uber withdraws from Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b67222f9bd508fe35c180af4f6bca78b60ce032195d65b11aae35aa8251052d6</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T20:39:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uber-withdraws-from-nigeria--7fddf4430022.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uber-withdraws-from-nigeria" /><summary type="html">In tonight's programme, a UN report says foreign fighters and support networks are fuelling Sudan’s war and worsening violence against civilians. Also, Uber is pulling out of Nigeria and Uganda, leaving thousands of drivers scrambling for new sources of income. And finally, we discuss the festival with co-director Diarah N’Daw-Spech and Laurence Cole, co-producer of the Nigerian film "Shadow of Greed".</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>‘Major potential breaches of British election law’: Inside Channel 4’s investigation into Reform UK</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c548cb09fa4d579be84371d503767a0f0b33d621fc0eb6f8b74898c8fa94add5</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T19:52:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260904-major-potential-breaches-of-british-election-law-understanding-channel-4-s-investigation--100a26e41120.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260904-major-potential-breaches-of-british-election-law-understanding-channel-4-s-investigation" /><summary type="html">Gavin Lee is pleased to welcome Peter Geoghegan, an award-winning investigative journalist. He's the editor of the Substack Democracy for Sale and the author of the best-selling book "Democracy for Sale". Geoghegan explains the significance of the Channel 4 investigation not simply over the conduct allegedly captured on camera, but in the broader question of how political influence is financed and made visible, or invisible, within British democracy.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>German power grid sabotage attack linked to ‘climate extremism’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d1d43083aaef8ec3800b3f2f38667fcb4232d0906a3c49b57310fd7a5a8c4a2</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:40:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-german-power-grid-sabotage-attack-linked-to-climate-extremism--b5a9f0391572.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-german-power-grid-sabotage-attack-linked-to-climate-extremism" /><summary type="html">German Interior Minister Alexander Dobrindt on Friday said the evidence in a recent spate of sabotage attacks on power grids across the country points to a militant climate activist.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UN ditches Mercator map to adopt more accurate one reflecting Africa's true size</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c276ec41e9651798e930d2603407214745c917201b2dcb74b124d674e9f8395b</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:31:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/earth/20260904-un-ditches-mercator-map-to-adopt-more-accurate-one-reflecting-africa-s-true-size--2bb05ca3b5d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/earth/20260904-un-ditches-mercator-map-to-adopt-more-accurate-one-reflecting-africa-s-true-size" /><summary type="html">The UN General Assembly on Friday voted to shift away from the 16th-century Mercator map, designed by Flemish cartographer Gerardus Mercator, for a more accurate one reflecting the true size of continents. The resolution, spearheaded by several African countries and co-sponsored by France, was backed by 164 countries. The US voted against and six other states abstained.</summary><category term="Earth" /></entry><entry><title>Germany’s ‘Most Dangerous Man’: PR gift for the AfD?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7b054b7361ca76acceb0a9a4e50290118165cc317568aa1d267bfccc159f481</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T18:31:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260904-germany-s-most-dangerous-man-pr-gift-for-the-afd--f852f5df9336.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260904-germany-s-most-dangerous-man-pr-gift-for-the-afd" /><summary type="html">The Ukrainian capital was hit by Russia’s most intense wave of air attacks on Kyiv, reportedly in four years, with Reuters describing air raid sirens, drones, cruise and ballistic missiles exhausting Ukraine’s defence system, with 12 people killed and the Ukrainian foreign minister making a direct appeal to Western allies for more Patriot interceptor missiles.</summary><category term="The World This Week" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's West Bank camp displacements could be crime against humanity, UN says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3813d55ba0601863bec275291dbfa6486a4c385125420d199039d87acf8be497</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T16:26:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-s-west-bank-camp-displacements-could-be-crime-against-humanity-un-says--03f625c09b2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-s-west-bank-camp-displacements-could-be-crime-against-humanity-un-says" /><summary type="html">The Israeli government's forced displacement of the entire populations of three West Bank refugee camps in January 2025 could amount to crimes against humanity, a UN report warned Friday. More than 33,000 Palestinians forced out of the Jenin, Nur Shams and Tulkarm camps have not been permitted to return home. Israel slammed the report for "spreading misinformation".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms start with North Carolina distributing mail-voting ballots</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a5c9432014534f64531fd113cdd23c721ab0a88c17325886a50dbe9b79bf263a</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:45Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:53:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-us-midterms-begin-with-chaos-over-mail-voting-crackdown--b948c78e1c61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-us-midterms-begin-with-chaos-over-mail-voting-crackdown" /><summary type="html">North Carolina on Friday became the first state authorised to begin sending out ballots, formally launching the 2026 US midterms as President Donald Trump’s administration fights to impose sweeping restrictions on the practice.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>'Italian opposition fragmented: No alternative leader, no other possible leader than Giorgia Meloni'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4e5e2537095f9d05ded4fbf0fe16e67695c515b65f488bb131fd891186b2627d</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:35:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italian-opposition-fragmented-no-alternative-leader-no-other-possible-leader-than-giorgia-m--1c36e6864261.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-italian-opposition-fragmented-no-alternative-leader-no-other-possible-leader-than-giorgia-meloni-1" /><summary type="html">Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Political analyst Lorenzo Pregliasco, co-founder of polling agency YouTrend and adjunct professor at the University of Bologna. He argues that Giorgia Meloni’s unusual longevity in office is best understood not simply as a record of political strength, but as the product of a carefully calibrated governing strategy. Meloni has maintained stability partly by avoiding structural reforms disruptive enough to mobilize multiple constituencies against her at once. Her dominance within Fratelli d’Italia, the absence of a credible alternative leader, and a fragmented opposition have reinforced that advantage.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider, the ideologist behind the AFD’s plans in Saxony-Anhalt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c55f3af4c110108fedd6a856a96c603fa6742ec79f3340cf1eddaf9ee64dbba2</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:34:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-germany-hans-thomas-tillschneider-the-ideologist-behind-the-afd-s-plans-in-saxony-anhalt--220beb71b19c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-germany-hans-thomas-tillschneider-the-ideologist-behind-the-afd-s-plans-in-saxony-anhalt" /><summary type="html">The far-right German political party Alternative for Germany could win a historical victory in the eastern state of Saxony-Anhalt in key elections this Sunday. The party’s agenda is more radical than ever and inspired by the proposals of an influential ideologist in the region: Hans-Thomas Tillschneider.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump envoys Witkoff, Kushner to visit Russia and Ukraine in coming days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dd2600a6440d67938a3e7b144d230df6f90920623291105c235a0309206c7a91</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:29:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-trump-envoys-witkoff-kushner-to-visit-russia-and-ukraine-in-coming-days--2d9b95db2738.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-trump-envoys-witkoff-kushner-to-visit-russia-and-ukraine-in-coming-days" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump's envoys Steve Witkoff and Jared Kushner are expected to arrive in Kyiv for a first-time visit on Sunday, several sources reported. Witkoff and Kushner – Trump's son-in-law – have been involved in shuttle diplomacy between Russia and Ukraine, travelling to Moscow multiple times, and are expected to visit Kyiv this weekend. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Commentator Kethevane Gorjestani tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>On the ground: Russian drone strikes Ukraine security service headquarters in Kyiv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:762029199a971897f2cc15e289b3f9a3cdf6d58c10f28caf8c0b365d1fc2ea10</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:24:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-on-the-ground-russian-drone-strikes-ukraine-security-service-headquarters-in-kyiv--af0328695810.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-on-the-ground-russian-drone-strikes-ukraine-security-service-headquarters-in-kyiv" /><summary type="html">A Russian drone struck the headquarters of Ukraine's SBU security services on Friday, Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky said, accusing Moscow of aiming directly at the SBU head's personal office. Zelensky said he had instructed the SBU to deliver an "appropriate, tangible response" to the strike, while Ukraine's Foreign Minister Andriy Sybiga described it as a "major escalation". FRANCE 24's Emmanuelle Chaze reports from Kyiv, Ukraine.</summary></entry><entry><title>US judge declares mistrial in Lindsay Clancy child-killing case after jury deadlock</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:16968be897579567b68a1d183da67ea7c2a0e4b18e26fd834eacafaf5b00e51b</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:41:48Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:21:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-judge-declares-mistrial-in-case-of-us-woman-who-killed-her-children--609fadb47579.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260904-judge-declares-mistrial-in-case-of-us-woman-who-killed-her-children" /><summary type="html">A judge in Massachusetts on Friday declared a mistrial in the Lindsay Clancy murder court case after jurors were unable to reach a unanimous verdict on her criminal responsibility for killing her three young children. The case sparked a public debate over maternal mental health.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Ethan Hawke leads the charge at Deauville's 52nd American Film Festival</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:857d386c98d7bb5f646ede4c15c2ca6915f3e61be674e9baa5fb1b3d0a34e811</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:19:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260904-ethan-hawke-leads-the-charge-at-deauville-s-52nd-american-film-festival--98a681434fde.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20260904-ethan-hawke-leads-the-charge-at-deauville-s-52nd-american-film-festival" /><summary type="html">The Normandy coast has become Hollywood-sur-mer once again, as the annual film festival welcomes talent from the United States. FRANCE 24's Genie Godula takes time out from hosting the opening ceremony in Deauville to bring us an overview of the features screening there.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>France announces €1 billion aid for farmers after climate-hit summer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8d8989f9dbcf9cb1032b381260cf7c8f10c562923f00db26daae9e857fdec066</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:12:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-france-announces-_1-billion-aid-for-farmers-after-climate-hit-summer--e6ed56d5d705.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-france-announces-%E2%82%AC1-billion-aid-for-farmers-after-climate-hit-summer" /><summary type="html">France has recorded its hottest summer on record this year as the country battled heatwaves, drought and massive wildfires. The extreme weather has continued into September, with France's national weather service placing five departments on orange alert for several days. Temperatures are expected to reach 40°C in some areas. France's agriculture minister also announced a plan to unlock over 1 billion euros in aid to the agriculture sector, which has been severely affected by the extreme weather.</summary></entry><entry><title>🔴 Russian drone ‘aimed directly’ at Ukraine security service HQ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c677778e7d1b91f4fbfcb1481ef70218593f3049637572c6ce6c7d1e8640d7b8</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:07:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-russian-drone-aimed-directly-at-ukraine-security-service-hq-zelensky-says--9847636126d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-russian-drone-aimed-directly-at-ukraine-security-service-hq-zelensky-says" /></entry><entry><title>Strengthening Africa is an investment in Europe's future: EU Commissioner Jozef Sikela</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:35e589d4818d44c9abb4a16570539b0068c08ceecec4be80831102062c885295</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T15:03:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-strengthening-africa-is-an-investment-in-europe-s-future-eu-commissioner-jozef-sikela--f05b28eefbd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-strengthening-africa-is-an-investment-in-europe-s-future-eu-commissioner-jozef-sikela" /><summary type="html">Are great-power politics back, at the expense of smaller countries? In an age of strongmen, is multilateralism in retreat? Not according to Jozef Sikela. The EU Commissioner in charge of International Partnerships insists that traditional multilateralism is alive and well, especially in the EU's approach to Africa and to the Arctic. We sat down with him for an interview at the European Commission in Brussels.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump administration unveils anti-immigration video games</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a87b3829286b15e575efdf69150f21d706a18fd753ee31363c980ec967b4a46</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T14:56:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-trump-administration-unveils-anti-immigration-video-games--e19dcf7f44fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-trump-administration-unveils-anti-immigration-video-games" /><summary type="html">The #arcade #games are unveiled as the #Trump administration steps up its mass #arrest and #deportation programme of undocumented #immigrants. According to recent data, most of those arrested in July by #ICE have no #criminal record.</summary></entry><entry><title>Himalayan hydropower buildout: Expert says risk management is key</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5db7d070d8665df5654f5e31b8315dd4b4d4e94fd66f6352fb0b3f7198f697be</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T14:34:07Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20260904-rebuilding-after-nepal-flash-floods-expert-says-risk-management-is-key-in-himalayas--1975b47e4597.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/access-asia/20260904-rebuilding-after-nepal-flash-floods-expert-says-risk-management-is-key-in-himalayas" /><summary type="html">Following devastating floods in Nepal and Tibet, Access Asia takes a closer look at the fragile state of the Himalayan mountains. Dr Arun Bhakta Shrestha, an expert on the environment and risk management in the Himalayas, explains why it's so difficult to detect glacier movements in advance and says that the tragedy could serve as an opportunity to improve the way nations develop infrastructure in the resource-rich region.</summary><category term="Access Asia" /></entry><entry><title>Russian drone strikes Ukraine security service HQ</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9df2a4843a833bff12cca77ba0fc8a49c9a569a0eb31a23a472486ad46260d63</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:59:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-russian-drone-aimed-directly-at-ukraine-security-service-hq-zelensky-says--9847636126d9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260904-russian-drone-aimed-directly-at-ukraine-security-service-hq-zelensky-says" /><summary type="html">A Russian drone struck the headquarters of Ukraine's SBU security services in Kyiv on Friday afternoon, said Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelensky, injuring five people. The attack followed a series of deadly overnight strikes across Ukraine, including the southern Odesa region.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>An inside look at Lucas Museum of Narrative Art in Los Angeles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61b745a7185373353a1a93a419e1636311acbb6efe0d663bd9976c71d3ffe52c</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:57:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-an-inside-look-at-lucas-museum-of-narrative-art-in-los-angeles--d22e94d7c5e9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-an-inside-look-at-lucas-museum-of-narrative-art-in-los-angeles" /><summary type="html">After years of delays and more than a billion dollars, the long-awaited Lucas Museum of Narrative Art is preparing to open its doors to the public in Los Angeles. The museum, founded by filmmaker George Lucas and his wife, businesswoman Mellody Hobson, will be a new home for visual storytelling spanning the Star Wars universe and beyond. FRANCE 24's correspondent Wassim Cornet reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nepal floods: Two workers pulled alive from tunnel after nine days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:00d3283d5a2d01db574844844a1ad26c7bbdc30b262ad1d4eb3da3edc0e407da</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:54:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-floods-two-workers-pulled-alive-from-tunnel-after-nine-days--5651e62af958.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-nepal-floods-two-workers-pulled-alive-from-tunnel-after-nine-days" /><summary type="html">Nepal's emergency crews have pulled two workers out of a hydropower tunnel where they had been trapped for nine days. The rescue comes more than a week after flash flooding along the Nepal-Tibet border killed more than 1,200 people. Both men have injuries to their hands and legs and have been airlifted to a hospital in Kathmandu for treatment.</summary></entry><entry><title>Meloni celebrates milestone as Italy's longest-lasting government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:23dd4769582f4e39b7bfb382f3657f1a3885774e4d4afe996231519ec303f467</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:50:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-meloni-celebrates-milestone-as-italy-s-longest-lasting-government--f397a1fc9a52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-meloni-celebrates-milestone-as-italy-s-longest-lasting-government" /><summary type="html">Italy's Prime Minister Giorgia Meloni is celebrating a milestone: her hard-right government is now the longest-lasting in the country's post war history. In a country known for its political instability, it's a notable record. But considerable challenges remain for Italy's first female prime minister, ahead of elections next year. FRANCE 24's Italy correspondent Seema Gupta reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Struggling to make its voice heard: Can the EU forge a true foreign policy?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47350997df927656698432a3959220efcea0eb89506089b1e418e84eb51f5437</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:42:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-struggling-to-make-its-voice-heard-can-the-eu-forge-a-true-foreign-policy--d3fdfae86cb4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/talking-europe/20260904-struggling-to-make-its-voice-heard-can-the-eu-forge-a-true-foreign-policy" /><summary type="html">"Who do I call if I want to speak to Europe?" The famous quote attributed to Henry Kissinger still resonates today. There is in fact a Mrs Europe on the world stage: Kaja Kallas, the EU High Representative for Foreign Affairs and Security Policy. She is actually the sixth high representative. But ever since that post was created, rivalries between different centres of power have diluted the EU's ability to speak with one voice. We saw that recently with tensions over who should represent the EU in any potential talks with Russia.</summary><category term="Talking Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli army has seized Lebanon's key Ali al-Taher ridge from Hezbollah</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b724ed5d751b469294e21fd43c7bc80fff506ad183ec96586988a8bc608cbd01</id><updated>2026-09-05T04:40:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:27:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-says-it-has-seized-lebanon-key-ali-al-taher-ridge-from-hezbollah--71676c0b7359.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-says-it-has-seized-lebanon-key-ali-al-taher-ridge-from-hezbollah" /><summary type="html">Israel has seized the strategically placed Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon from Hezbollah fighters, Defence Minister Israel Katz said Friday. The Iran-aligned Shiite group did not confirm losing the highland, which sits around 10 kilometres from the border with Israel and was pummelled by Israeli strikes in recent weeks despite a ceasefire.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
